      "attempt_id": "B_transitive_attempt_2",
      "message": "2` and the original `can_transition` body `return (old,new) in {('new','paid'),('new','cancelled'),('paid','refunded')}` \u2014 explicitly noting the semantics are duplicated rather than imported.\n- `CONTRACT_VERSION = 2` mirrored as a module constant.\n- `VALID_TRANSITIONS = frozenset({(\"new\",\"paid\"), (\"new\",\"cancelled\"), (\"paid\",\"refunded\")})`.\n- `can_transition(old, new)` \u2014 membership test against `VALID_TRANSITIONS`, identical semantics to contract v2.\n- `consume(old, new)` \u2014 the requested entry point; delegates to `can_transition`, returning `True` only for the three allowed v2 transitions and `False` for unknown states, self-transitions, and transitions out of terminal states (`paid`\u2192`cancelled`, `refunded`\u2192anything, `cancelled`\u2192anything).\n\nNo import of `semkg_contract` and no `sys.path` dependence on it; the file is self-contained. No other files under the attempt directory were created (a temporary probe file attempt did not land in the attempt dir, so nothing extra was left behind)."
